<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><BaseHead title="Privacy — Paisa" description="How Paisa handles your financial context." /></head><body><main class="legal-page"><a href="/">← Back to Paisa</a><span class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</span><h1>Your financial context belongs to you.</h1><p class="lead">Paisa stores only the information needed to organize your spending and complete daily reviews. Records are isolated by authenticated account.</p><h2>What we store</h2><p>Your account identifier, transaction data you import, review explanations, groups, reminder preferences, and limited security audit events.</p><h2>How it is used</h2><p>To build your review queue, prevent duplicate reminders, generate spending summaries, and keep your progress synchronized. Paisa does not sell financial data or use it for advertising.</p><h2>Your controls</h2><p>You can export a portable copy or permanently delete your account data from Preferences. Deletion removes transactions, reviews, groups, and preferences.</p><h2>Security</h2><p>Access is authenticated, data queries are scoped to the current user, and sensitive responses are not cached. Provider credentials are stored as deployment secrets rather than in application source.</p><p class="legal-note">Last updated: 2 August 2026. Before a public commercial launch, this notice should be reviewed for the jurisdictions and financial-data providers you select.</p></main></body></html>
